# Secrets - NEVER commit
API-Key-*.txt
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Desktop app data lives INSIDE this project folder on this machine
# (C:\LegionWallpaper\Claude\). It is app data, not project content - NEVER
# track it.
/Claude/

# Local-only Claude Code / MCP config. RC ignored the whole .claude/ tree;
# LW tracks .claude/ itself (settings.json, commands/, agents/ are project
# content) and ignores only the machine-local pieces, preserving RC's intent
# that per-machine config, tokens, and worktree checkouts never get tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
.claude/worktrees/
.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp/

# Audit-cleanup quarantine (move-not-delete pattern; safe to rm after
# stability confirmed)
_archive/

# Scratch / session-debug logs (pytest output, wakeup snapshots, iter loggings)
_scratch/

# Operator's living work list - Claude-synced, untracked one-stop tracker
LW_WORK_TRACKER.md

# Image pipeline content - the operator's personal image corpus (GBs of
# binaries). The PROCESS is shareable and tracked (tools/, docs/,
# .claude/commands/); the images themselves never are. Track only the
# folder skeleton via .gitkeep so a fresh clone has the stage tree.
images/**
!images/**/
!images/**/.gitkeep

# Root pipeline status log - per-image transition history for THIS
# machine's corpus. Untracked like LW_WORK_TRACKER.md (personal state,
# not shareable process).
PIPELINE_LOG.md

# Databases - never commit binary DB files.
# Recursive on purpose - a bare `data/*.db` only catches direct children.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Logs (daily rotating - logs/YYYY-MM-DD.log convention)
logs/

# Runtime state (mutates constantly)
ops/runtime/
restart_trigger.txt

# Gemini director/auditor loop runtime droppings (sentinels, controller.log,
# directive.md, directive_history.jsonl, budget.json, _gemini_* transcripts).
# Track only the .gitkeep placeholder so the control dir exists on checkout.
ops/loop/control/*
!ops/loop/control/.gitkeep

# Sync staging
tmp/

# Audit/snapshot tarballs
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Python bytecode + caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Python virtual environments - ML side-venvs (torch cu128 / pyiqa stacks,
# multi-GB; one venv per tool family per RESTORATION_PLAN.md). Never commit.
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/

# Downloaded upscaler model weights (IllustrationJaNai DAT2/ESRGAN etc.,
# 100s of MB each; fetched per RESTORATION_PLAN.md section 3, licensing
# re-check queued). The pipeline downloads them; they are never committed.
# Keep the folder on checkout via .gitkeep.
tools/models/*
!tools/models/.gitkeep

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.obsidian/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Profiling output
*.prof
*.lprof

# Node (if any future tooling)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Ad-hoc diagnostic artefacts under data/. Leading dot keeps them sorted
# to the top of the dir + signals "transient debug output, not persistent
# state".
data/.*.png
data/.*.json
data/.*.jsonl
data/.*.tmp

# Golden-set image bytes (privacy). The manifest data/golden/*.json IS tracked
# (the shareable proof-of-process); the input + baseline image bytes are not -
# they are sha-pinned in the manifest. See docs/research/GOLDEN_SET.md.
data/golden/inputs/
data/golden/baseline/

# Source-recovery fetched image bytes (privacy - same boundary as golden/ and
# images/**). gallery-dl / manual downloads land third-party art on this box;
# NEVER commit it. The recovery METADATA (manual_queue.csv, hashes/matches
# JSON caches, logs) IS trackable process state and stays. See
# docs/research/SOURCE_RECOVERY.md section 5. Keep the dir on checkout via
# .gitkeep; ignore any downloaded image bytes and the fetch subdir.
data/recovery/downloads/
data/recovery/*.jpg
data/recovery/*.jpeg
data/recovery/*.png
data/recovery/*.webp
data/recovery/*.gif

# Transient verify/test scratch dropped at repo root by item runs
# (_verify_*.txt and friends) + ad-hoc stdout/stderr captures.
/_*.txt
_verify_*.txt
/*_out.log
/*_err.log
